    <section>
    <p> Have you ever attempted to cancel a subscription and found it difficult or frustrating? This is a common example of a dark pattern in UX design.</p>
    <p> Dark patterns in UX design are deceptive or manipulative techniques used by websites or companies to subtly influence users into performing actions they might not otherwise take.</p>
    <p> These techniques tend to exploit psychological principles and tendencies to encourage behaviors that will often be detrimental to the user, but beneficial to the company.</p>
    <p> Dark patterns can be difficult to detect because they rely on subtle design elements that take advantage of user's expectations, habits, or experiences with standard UX design.</p>
    </section>
